# `table.get(q)` and `table.has(q)` find the same in every iteration and are hoisted. A lookup hashes its key, and flattens it if it is a rope, so a loop that never iterates must not pay for it.
# The generic version is printed first. The preheader of the specialized version makes the header's own test on the values that enter: it has no position in the source. Where it fails, the generic version runs.
# Nothing proves that `n` is a number, so the test is the one that the specialized header makes, against its own integer bound. Both lookups follow where it passes: the test is made once.
# RUN: walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK: ) isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true:
# CHECK: ) isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true:
# CHECK: form=Integers # uses=1
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch
# CHECK: ():
# CHECK-NEXT: = Unbox
# CHECK-NEXT: inlineBuiltin=MapGet
# CHECK-NOT: Branch
# CHECK: inlineBuiltin=MapHas
# CHECK-NEXT: Jump -> next
# CHECK-NOT: inlineBuiltin=Map
# -- source: hoisted-lookup-follows-the-loop-entry-test.ts
